# Line-ending policy.
#
# LinkBank is built and run on Linux (the Docker image, and the TrueNAS host),
# so every text file should use LF in the repo and in the working tree — even
# when cloned on Windows. This keeps shell scripts executable on the Linux side
# and prevents spurious whitespace-only diffs when contributors are on different
# operating systems. It overrides any local `core.autocrlf` setting.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Scripts that MUST stay LF (they run under bash on Linux / in the container).
*.sh   text eol=lf

# Binary assets — never normalized or touched.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.ico  binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
